{"step_index":802,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:00:59Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. Create a function `generate_tax_suggestions(audit_summary, calculated_tax)` using Gemini 2.5 Flash:\n\nInput Context:\n- Total turnover and deemed profit (calculated by code)\n- Number of invoices analyzed\n- Total GST paid on purchases (potential ITC)\n- Invoices missing GSTIN (disallowed ITC)\n\nPrompt the model with:\n\"You are a tax preparation assistant for small Indian retail shopkeepers.\nGiven this pre-calculated financial data:\n{data}\n\nProvide 3 concise bullet points:\n1. Recommended ITR Form: (e.g., ITR-4 Sugam under Sec 44AD vs ITR-3) with a 1-sentence reason.\n2. GST ITC Opportunity / Risk: Explain how much Input Tax Credit can be claimed from audited bills and warn about unverified supplier GSTINs.\n3. Advance Tax & Action Item: Remind them of the March 15 advance tax deadline.\n\nTone: Grounded, simple English, no complex jargon. Include a clear disclaimer: 'Not tax advice; verify with your CA.'\"\n\nUI Dashboard AdditionIn your React frontend, add a \"Tax & ITR Insights\" tab or summary card right below the invoice audit report:Pill 1: Recommended Form: ITR-4 (Presumptive Scheme - Sec 44AD)Pill 2: Deemed Net Profit: ₹X,XX,XXX (Calculated at 6% digital / 8% cash)Pill 3: Estimated Tax Liability: ₹X,XXX (Computed via New Regime)Advisory Callout Box: Plain-English summary explaining how keeping supplier GSTINs verified maximizes their Input Tax Credit and reduces tax outgo.   \n2. great now make the app functioning with real time bills and calculations based on inputs with the suitable outputs\n3. You are an invoice parsing engine for AUDIT IT.\n\nTASK:\n1. Examine the provided document or image.\n2. First, determine if this is a genuine business invoice, cash memo, purchase bill, or tax receipt.\n3. IF IT IS NOT an invoice (e.g. it is a person's photo, landscape, screenshot of a chat, unrelated document, or random text):\n   - Set `is_valid_bill` to false.\n   - Set `rejection_reason` explaining why (e.g. \"Uploaded image is not a financial bill or invoice\").\n   - Leave all financial fields null or empty.\n4. IF IT IS AN INVOICE:\n   - Set `is_valid_bill` to true.\n   - Extract the fields as accurately as possible.\n   - NEVER make up or hallucinate missing data. If a field (like GSTIN or invoice number) is not present or unreadable, set it to null and append it to `unreadable_fields`.\n\nmake the app strictly calculate and analyse the given inputs with precision \n4. without changing the rest core features, fix the issue that original uploaded document does not match with digitized parcha shown , it currently displaying random items irrelevant to the given invoice\n5. if something seems missing or is unclear in the given document then do not move ahead and calculate just simply ask the user to give valid input \n6. CRITICAL PARSING RULES:\n1. HEADER VS TABLE SEPARATION:\n   - Metadata in the header or footer (Supplier Name, Address, Contact/Phone Number, GSTIN, PAN, Invoice Number, Date, Bank Details) MUST NEVER be extracted as line items.\n   - The `items` array MUST ONLY contain tangible goods, products, or billed services listed within the invoice's central itemized table.\n\n2. EXCLUSION RULES FOR ITEMS:\n   - NEVER create a line item for a GSTIN (e.g., 15-character alphanumeric strings like '06AAECM4821F1ZX').\n   - NEVER create a line item for a Phone / Mobile / Contact Number.\n   - Every valid item MUST represent a product or service with a genuine unit quantity and unit price. If a row lacks a product description or represents invoice metadata, ignore it from `items`.\n\nimport re\n\ndef clean_extracted_items(items: list) -> list:\n    cleaned = []\n    \n    # Pattern matching GSTIN (15 characters: 2 digits, 5 letters, 4 digits, 1 letter, 1 digit/letter, Z, 1 digit/letter)\n    gstin_pattern = re.compile(r'\\b\\d{2}[A-Z]{5}\\d{4}[A-Z]{1}[1-9A-Z]{1}Z[0-9A-Z]{1}\\b', re.IGNORECASE)\n    # Pattern matching Indian phone numbers (10 digits, optional +91 prefix)\n    phone_pattern = re.compile(r'(\\+?91[\\-\\s]?)?[6-9]\\d{9}')\n    \n    # Common metadata keywords that should never be product names\n    forbidden_keywords = [\n        \"gstin\", \"gst no\", \"contact\", \"phone\", \"mobile\", \"tel\", \n        \"pan no\", \"bank\", \"ifsc\", \"account no\", \"invoice no\"\n    ]\n\n    for item in items:\n        desc = item.get(\"description\", \"\").strip()\n        desc_lower = desc.lower()\n\n        # 1. Skip if the description contains GSTIN patterns or phone numbers\n        if gstin_pattern.search(desc) or phone_pattern.search(desc):\n         \n<truncated 643 bytes>\n7. You are an invoice OCR parser for Indian GST tax invoices.\n\nMANDATORY RULES:\n1. SUPPLIER NAME:\n   - Extract ONLY the business trade name or company name (e.g., 'Modern Electrical & Hardware', 'Sharma Enterprises').\n   - NEVER include phone numbers, email addresses, or 'Phone: ...' in the supplier_name field.\n\n2. WHAT IS A LINE ITEM:\n   - An item MUST be an actual product, part, material, or service from the invoice's item table (e.g., 'LED Tube Light 20W', 'Basmati Rice 25kg').\n   - An item MUST have a valid product name, quantity > 0, unit rate > 0, and item total.\n\n3. ABSOLUTE FORBIDDEN LINE ITEMS (DO NOT EXTRACT THESE AS ITEMS):\n   - Street addresses, plots, industrial area names (e.g. 'Plot No...', 'Industrial Area', 'Main Bazaar', 'Sonipat').\n   - Buyer/Seller GSTIN or PAN strings (e.g. '06AAECM...', 'BZKPALZD...').\n   - Pincodes or telephone numbers.\n   - Amount in words (e.g. 'Thirteen Thousand Nine Hundred...').\n   - Bank account details, IFSC codes, payment terms.\n\nIf a line of text is not a physical item or billed service inside the central table, DISCARD IT. Do not guess.\n```\"\n\n\nAdd this cleaning function to the backend and run it on extracted_data immediately before sending it to the frontend:\"\n\nPython\nimport re\n\ndef sanitize_invoice_data(data: dict) -> dict:\n    # 1. Clean Supplier Name (Remove phone/email artifacts)\n    supplier = data.get(\"vendor_name\", \"\") or \"\"\n    supplier_cleaned = re.sub(r'(Phone|Mobile|Tel|Email|Mob)[\\s:]*[\\+\\d\\s\\w@\\.\\-]+', '', supplier, flags=re.IGNORECASE).strip()\n    data[\"vendor_name\"] = supplier_cleaned if supplier_cleaned else \"Supplier Name Unclear\"\n\n    # 2. Filter out non-items from the items list\n    filtered_items = []\n    \n    # Com\n<truncated 1251 bytes>\n8. Replace the invoice upload backend endpoint completely with this robust FastAPI + Google GenAI implementation:\n\n1. Accept the file via UploadFile.\n2. Read the raw bytes and pass them directly as an inline image/PDF to 'gemini-2.5-flash'.\n3. Use this exact Pydantic schema and system prompt:\n\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom google import genai\nfrom google.genai import types\n\nclass InvoiceItem(BaseModel):\n    description: str\n    quantity: float\n    unit_rate: float\n    total_amount: float\n\nclass ExtractedInvoice(BaseModel):\n    is_valid_bill: bool\n    vendor_name: Optional[str]\n    gstin: Optional[str]\n    invoice_number: Optional[str]\n    date: Optional[str]\n    items: List[InvoiceItem]\n    subtotal: Optional[float]\n    cgst: Optional[float]\n    sgst: Optional[float]\n    igst: Optional[float]\n    declared_total: Optional[float]\n\n@app.post(\"/api/analyze-bill\")\nasync def analyze_bill(file: UploadFile = File(...)):\n    contents = await file.read()\n    mime_type = file.content_type or \"image/jpeg\"\n    \n    prompt = \"\"\"\n    Extract all billing details from this Indian tax invoice/cash bill.\n    RULES:\n    1. Extract vendor name (company title only, no phone numbers).\n    2. Extract only valid goods/services into the `items` list. DO NOT include addresses, phone numbers, or pincodes as items.\n    3. Read numeric amounts carefully. Do not invent items.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    response = client.models.generate_content(\n        model='gemini-2.5-flash',\n        contents=[\n            types.Part.from_bytes(data=contents, mime_type=mime_type),\n            prompt\n        ],\n        config=types.GenerateContentConfig(\n            response_mime_type=\"application/json\",\n \n<truncated 113 bytes>\n9.  CRITICAL BUG FIX: Remove the gatekeeper check that is rejecting valid invoices.\n\n1. REMOVE `is_valid_bill` and any checks that reject documents.\n2. In the Gemini prompt, DO NOT ask the model to evaluate if it is a bill. Simply instruct it:\n   \"Extract the invoice details from this image/document into JSON:\n    - vendor_name: (string)\n    - gstin: (string or null)\n    - invoice_number: (string or null)\n    - items: list of {description, quantity, unit_rate, total_amount}\n    - subtotal: (number)\n    - cgst: (number)\n    - sgst: (number)\n    - igst: (number)\n    - declared_total: (number)\n    If any field is missing or unclear, leave it null. Do not include addresses or phone numbers as line items.\"\n3. REMOVE the fallback that generates dummy ₹1.00 items when an error happens. Always use the actual data returned by Gemini.\n\njust get the data by gemini using  this API key\n AQ.Ab8RN6LhTNa6kIQRpd_OijgrXNfmwLOw7rcxiMN8aWW-_U7mPw\n10.     Fix the table column alignment and extraction accuracy in the invoice parser:\n\n1. Update the Gemini extraction prompt with these table-parsing rules:\n   \"TABLE COLUMN ALIGNMENT INSTRUCTIONS:\n    - Carefully identify the table header row to locate column boundaries (S.No, Description, HSN/SAC, Quantity, Unit, Rate/Price, Amount).\n    - CROSS-CHECK MATH INTERNALLY: For each row, verify that (quantity * unit_rate) roughly equals the row total amount. \n      * If quantity * rate does not equal the row amount, you likely swapped the Quantity and Rate columns, or confused the Item Code/HSN/S.No with Quantity. \n      * Never set Rate to trivial numbers like 1 or 2 when the item is an expensive product like a 'Tool Kit', unless that is explicitly the printed unit rate.\n    - Clean description: Do not append units like 'NO', 'PCS', 'NOS', or serial numbers into the product description.\"\n\n2. Post-Processing Column Swap Fallback (Python):\n   Add a quick sanity check in the backend:\n   for item in items:\n       qty = item.get('quantity', 0)\n       rate = item.get('unit_rate', 0)\n       total = item.get('total_amount', 0)\n       \n       # If total matches qty exactly and rate is small (e.g. qty=535, rate=2, total=535), \n       # it means qty and rate were misaligned. Swap them:\n       if total > 0 and qty == total and rate in [1, 2]:\n           item['quantity'] = 1.0\n           item['unit_rate'] = total\n\n<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **Goal:** Build and enhance \"AUDIT IT\", a modern, trustworthy web app for Indian small retail shop owners to audit purchase bills, check arithmetic accuracy (Quantity $\\times$ Rate, GST, Grand Total), calculate Sec 44AD presumptive tax metrics, and perform AI-driven extraction via Gemini (`gemini-2.5-flash` / `gemini-3.5-flash`).\n   - **Latest User Request:**\n     1. Update the Gemini extraction prompt with **TABLE COLUMN ALIGNMENT INSTRUCTIONS**:\n        - Locate column boundaries (S.No, Description, HSN/SAC, Quantity, Unit, Rate/Price, Amount).\n        - Cross-check math internally: verify $(quantity \\times unit\\_rate) \\approx row\\_total\\_amount$. If not equal, swapped columns or confused Item Code/HSN/S.No with Quantity. Never set Rate to trivial numbers like 1 or 2 when the item is expensive (e.g. 'Tool Kit') unless explicitly printed.\n        - Clean description: Do not append units like 'NO', 'PCS', 'NOS', or serial numbers into the product description.\n     2. Add **Post-Processing Column Swap Fallback (Python)** in backend:\n        ```python\n        for item in items:\n            qty = item.get('quantity', 0)\n            rate = item.get('unit_rate', 0)\n            total = item.get('total_amount', 0)\n            if total > 0 and qty == total and rate in [1, 2]:\n                item['quantity'] = 1.0\n                item['unit_rate'] = total\n        ```\n     3. Ensure the active API key is set to: `AQ.Ab8RN6LhTNa6kIQRpd_OijgrXNfmwLOw7rcxiMN8aWW-_U7mPw`.\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Workspace Directory:** `/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it`\n   - **Server:** FastAPI server running on `http://localhost:3000` via daemon task `f7fe8eca-ba38-4dcb-97a7-a40aeb890237/task-762` using `/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/venv/bin/python3`.\n   - **Completed Edits:**\n     - `server.py`:\n       - Prompt updated with exact `TABLE COLUMN ALIGNMENT INSTRUCTIONS`.\n       - Added post-processing column swap check: `if total > 0 and qty == total and rate in [1, 2, 1.0, 2.0]: item['quantity'] = 1.0; item['unit_rate'] = total`.\n       - Removed `is_valid_bill` from `ExtractedInvoice` schema.\n       - Configured `DEFAULT_GEMINI_API_KEY = \"AQ.Ab8RN6LhTNa6kIQRpd_OijgrXNfmwLOw7rcxiMN8aWW-_U7mPw\"`.\n       - Automatic model fallback from `gemini-2.5-flash` to `gemini-3.5-flash` if 404/retired.\n     - `utils/clean_items.py`:\n       - Added post-processing column swap check in `clean_extracted_items` and `sanitize_invoice_data`.\n       - Added regex to trim unit words (`NO|NOS|PCS|PIECES|PKT|PACKET|KG|BOX|SET`) from product descriptions.\n     - `utils/aiExtractor.js`:\n       - Updated `GEMINI_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION` with table column alignment instructions.\n       - Removed dummy ₹1.00 / fake item generation and `is_valid_bill: false` rejection logic.\n       - Configured default key `AQ.Ab8RN6LhTNa6kIQRpd_OijgrXNfmwLOw7rcxiMN